WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.950 --> 00:00:02.083
(light electronic music)

00:00:02.083 --> 00:00:05.848
- [Host] This is Jubal,
an Eastern Black Rhino.

00:00:05.848 --> 00:00:10.015
Coming in at around 2,690
pounds, big is an understatement.

00:00:11.989 --> 00:00:15.332
But with less than 740 left in the wild,

00:00:15.332 --> 00:00:17.890
the Eastern Black Rhino is
one of the rarest rhinos

00:00:17.890 --> 00:00:18.973
in the world.

00:00:23.957 --> 00:00:28.440
Jubal is 20 years old and
stands close to 12 feet long.

00:00:28.440 --> 00:00:31.474
They are solitary animals
with an aggressive disposition

00:00:31.474 --> 00:00:33.828
to discourage predators.

00:00:33.828 --> 00:00:35.911
They may seem tranquil,
but they will charge first

00:00:35.911 --> 00:00:37.744
and investigate later.

00:00:41.480 --> 00:00:44.152
Black Rhinos are browsers,
and eat leafy plants,

00:00:44.152 --> 00:00:46.642
branches, shoots, and
whatever else they can find

00:00:46.642 --> 00:00:49.948
in the highland and Savannah habitats.

00:00:49.948 --> 00:00:52.212
His large ears can
rotate to pick up sounds

00:00:52.212 --> 00:00:53.962
from many directions.

00:00:56.332 --> 00:00:58.023
Today, Eastern Black Rhinos

00:00:58.023 --> 00:01:00.264
are only left in Kenya and Tanzania.

00:01:00.264 --> 00:01:03.026
The population has declined by 90%

00:01:03.026 --> 00:01:05.693
over the last three generations.

00:01:06.537 --> 00:01:08.595
The biggest threat for
these guys are humans,

00:01:08.595 --> 00:01:12.762
as poaching has absolutely
devastated their population.

00:01:14.867 --> 00:01:17.534
This is the Eastern Black Rhino.

